{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX LANDED FOR REVIEW — Gerrit change 1587, stacked on 1586 (the b2bb split that unblocked it).\n\nThe fix is the one identified in the prior session's root-cause comment, applied to\n_compact_locked in its new home (compact_txn.py, which has real headroom now):\nsource_uuids skips any folded file whose basename — after stripping RETIRED_SUFFIX — ends\nin -SNAPSHOT.json. The normal path now agrees with the rebuild path, which already skipped\nsnapshots.\n\nHELD-OUT TEST — tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_snapshot_source_uuids_aea0.py\nAsserts BOTH directions, because AC3 requires the b636 guard not be weakened:\n  1. compact twice; the second SNAPSHOT must NOT cite the first SNAPSHOT's uuid, and must\n     still cite the raw event folded in the same pass (no over-correction);\n  2. delete a retired RAW source a snapshot cites — fsck must STILL report\n     SNAPSHOT_MISSING_SOURCES.\n\nPROVEN by reverting the single expression to its old form: assertion 1 fails with 'the\nsuperseded SNAPSHOT was cited as a source event', assertion 2 passes UNCHANGED in both\nstates. That is the evidence that the change is targeted at the false positive and does not\nloosen the truncated-log guard.\n\nAC STATUS\n- [x] snapshot_missing_sources no longer counts a cited uuid whose event is a superseded\n      SNAPSHOT. Determined WITHOUT a history walk — the compactor already knows which files\n      it is folding, so the filename suffix is authoritative at that point.\n- [ ] The six listed tickets report clean afterwards, status unchanged. NOT YET VERIFIABLE:\n      they self-heal on their NEXT compaction, which cannot happen until 1587 merges and the\n      local build picks it up. Re-check with fsck after it lands before closing.\n- [x] A genuinely missing raw event is still reported — held-out test, both directions.\n- [ ] 'Consider recording the folded snapshot uuid distinctly in the SNAPSHOT payload so the\n      distinction is structural rather than inferred.' NOT DONE, deliberately: it is a\n      payload/schema change affecting every future snapshot, and the filename suffix is\n      already authoritative at fold time. Worth its own ticket if the structural form is\n      wanted; it is not needed to fix this bug.\n\nDO NOT CLOSE until 1587 is Verified +1 and merged, and the six tickets are re-checked."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786383007386206001,"uuid":"dce67125-a964-463e-9ff8-e8dd35535c46"}